I looked at testing the `0x48 BASEFEE` opcode. Solidity PR was waiting to make sure the fork went okay. The other method was to use `verbatim` in Yul, but that is not available as an inline yet.

So I think you can do it, by deploying a `.yul` contract with the function:

```
{
    function basefee() -> out {
        out := verbatim_0i_1o(hex"48")
    }

    sstore(0, basefee())
}
```

https://github.com/ethereum/solidity/pull/11647#issuecomment-891805433

Which I tried to do in Hardhat, but didn't manage to get `.yul` contracts to compile there.
